ation/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d032f85503ffbc66ca0b3282a2670491ed5d0d1acfbccd58be0462a4e7059351","event_uuid":"fececf9c-8d1c-49eb-b214-acef00bfd997","position":{"commit_sha":"623c181567490d9f291be41dbb779dcc2c8b195f","position":"1787373940972980001-fececf9c-8d1c-49eb-b214-acef00bfd997"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix pushed as Gerrit change 2055 (commit 3e71c6d70f). RED->GREEN: 4 tests seen failing on the old fail-open behaviour, then the INFRA arm now abstains — verdict becomes INDETERMINATE (never weakening an existing BLOCK), no advisory that reads as a pass; coverage keeps carrying the classification error/reason. Gates green locally: pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py (40 passed), test_review_bot.py -k indeterminate (3 passed), full test_review_bot.py + retrigger suite (112 passed), make lint, make typecheck, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1.","timestamp":1787368649039592001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verification: Gerrit change 2055 merged to main as f6d937caf9607ed38639f45ea220144033703f87 with LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot, 1 non-blocking advisory) and Verified +1 (CI run 32548555272, all jobs green incl. pytest 3.11-3.13 on ubuntu+macos, lint+typecheck, mutation shard selection). Bug class: preexisting (fail-open design in the original ad0d B2 gate). The INFRA arm now abstains (INDETERMINATE) instead of degrading to advisory; classification error/reason remain in coverage.bugfix_size_gate for the infra-recovery loop.","timestamp":1787373940972980001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787354597536923001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"00daf4e1-2db9-49a3-b4c5-68c74b4d0c04","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1dd5-1880-17d0-4ac0"},{"link_uuid":"922e725b-08e9-4e36-b9c2-f8c251a14be4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eca9-cfbe-0556-465d"},{"link_uuid":"523e97d2-e656-47b1-86f9-bdaf962a384d","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"ad0d-6338-bc8c-43b6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` requires a plan-review attestation for a bug fix over 150 non-test lines. When the attestation classification itself raises (`classify_plan_review_attestation` catches every exception and returns `verdict: \"error\"`), `apply_bugfix_size_gate` maps INFRA to an **advisory** finding (module docstring: \"Fail-open on infrastructure\") and the change keeps `LLM-Review +1`. An infrastructure fault therefore produces the same outcome as a satisfied gate.\n\n## Reproduction\n- Gerrit change 1369 (`73abb5805f`, trailer ticket e39f, type bug, 525 non-test lines) merged on `LLM-Review +1` with 0 blocking / 2 advisory findings; the REVIEW_RESULT coverage records the bugfix-size gate as `error`. The ticket `asbestos-lithe-kouprey` (b6e1-c217-8cd3-4446) was later filed against that change.\n- Unit: make `_load_ticket_state` raise inside `classify_plan_review_attestation`; `apply_bugfix_size_gate` leaves `verdict` unchanged from PASS.\n\n## Expected\nAn infrastructure error in a blocking gate abstains instead of passing: the verdict becomes INDETERMINATE, with the classification error surfaced in the coverage record (`coverage.bugfix_size_gate.verdict == \"error\"`). Downstream (existing behaviour, unchanged by this fix): the review-bot adapter maps a non-PASS verdict with no blocking findings to the `indeterminate` coverage gap and the voter casts the fail-closed `-1` tagged as infrastructure — never a `+1` — so an unclassifiable oversized bug fix can no longer merge on the gate's silence. This is the same fail-closed-on-infra posture the codebase already established (bug 3fce: an unreadable ruling is an error, never a silent degrade; WS5 `detectors.apply_failclosed`).\n\n## Approach\nChange only the INFRA arm of `apply_bugfix_size_gate`: instead of appending an advisory finding, set `verdict[\"verdict\"] = \"INDETERMINATE\"` (never downgrading an existing BLOCK). The coverage entry (already written for every bucket) keeps carrying the `error` verdict and reason, so the bot's infra-recovery/retrigger loop can observe why. Leave the `flag` (BLOCK) and `accepted` (no-op) arms, the ≤150-line no-op, and the missing-trailer no-op unchanged. Update the module docstring (`Fail-open on infrastructure` → fail-closed abstain), `bucket_for_verdict`'s docstring, and the stale caller comment in `finalize.py`.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py` — the INFRA arm + docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py` — the call-site comment only.\n- `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py` — new RED test for the INDETERMINATE outcome; rewrite the two tests that encoded the old fail-open behaviour (`test_infra_or_unknown_classification_is_advisory_never_blocks`, `test_classifier_exception_degrades_to_advisory`); a guard test that an already-BLOCK verdict is not downgraded.\n\n## Testing\n- RED first: classification error on a >150-line non-test bug-fix diff yields `verdict == \"INDETERMINATE\"`, a coverage entry `bugfix_size_gate.verdict == \"error\"` / `bucket == \"infra\"`, and no advisory or blocking finding that reads as a pass.\n- Edge: an infra classification when the verdict is already BLOCK leaves BLOCK in place.\n- Unchanged behaviour: `unsigned`/`stale-material` still BLOCK, accepted verdicts still no-op, under-floor and test-only diffs never read the store.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A classification error (both the classifier's own `error` verdict and an exception escaping to the gate's outer handler) on an over-floor bug fix produces an INDETERMINATE review verdict, not PASS; checked by the new unit tests in `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`.\n- [x] An infra classification never downgrades an existing BLOCK verdict; checked by a new unit test.\n- [x] Existing tests for `unsigned`, certified/stale-code/stale-head, under-floor, test-only, non-bug, and unresolvable-ticket behaviour pass unchanged; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`.\n- [x] The Gerrit voter's existing INDETERMINATE handling (terminal fail-closed `-1`, no `+1`) is unchanged; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k indeterminate`.\n\n## Verification\n`pytest tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k \"bugfix_size or indeterminate\"`; `make lint`; `make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py","reason":"INFRA arm abstains (INDETERMINATE) instead of advisory; docstrings updated"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","reason":"call-site comment no longer claims infra degrades to advisory"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py","reason":"RED test for INDETERMINATE on classification error; rewrite the two fail-open tests; BLOCK-not-downgraded guard"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1dd5-1880-17d0-4ac0"],["relates_to","eca9-cfbe-0556-465d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"02e47778-96eb-47b0-9bb6-3b39e53566bb","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["gates","code-review","fail-open","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"9011-54d6-eb04-4cd6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"bugfix-size attestation gate degrades to advisory on classification error, so an infra fault passes the change","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["00daf4e1-2db9-49a3-b4c5-68c74b4d0c04","2a11a9c0-4644-4c2b-a153-3fdd402d981a","af1f6562-cec5-448d-854d-a1e0aafeb91a","d6e24409-e1bd-4c5e-9731-d9fc7dd08f8b","65b0e074-a6da-4a6f-80e7-20e5bb6883c6","14fea8d2-1162-4442-9547-35525e29f2d0","c89e5ce5-547d-43a1-bd0a-5cddabfd4b9b","922e725b-08e9-4e36-b9c2-f8c251a14be4","26431f02-6386-4b63-9a75-f1a63a93ebd0","02e47778-96eb-47b0-9bb6-3b39e53566bb","bf7d41fb-be21-4dcb-9f8a-db4deb870a7b","523e97d2-e656-47b1-86f9-bdaf962a384d","fececf9c-8d1c-49eb-b214-acef00bfd997"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787378791615696495,"uuid":"52c37e93-604e-42b4-82fc-fd4e5e216d73"}